{"id":"days-to-issue","title":"Days from filing to permit, by kind and year","question":"How long does a permit take, and how many applications die waiting?","finding":"Full-review alteration permits issued in 2019 took a median 292 days from filing; in 2023, 328; in 2025, 173. New buildings issued in 2025 took a median 711 days. 2,261 full-review applications filed 2015 to 2023 (11.1%) were withdrawn, cancelled or expired after a year or more without ever being issued, and 2,250 filed by 2023 are still waiting.","how":"Days from the filed date to the issued date (the day fees are paid and the permit is handed over), grouped by the year of issue. 'Died waiting' counts applications never issued whose last status is withdrawn, cancelled, expired or disapproved and whose last status date is a year or more after filing.","limits":"Issue date trails approval when the applicant is slow to pay. A project can be withdrawn because financing fell through, not because of the City. Since January 2024 planning approval and the building permit are filed separately, which shortens the building-permit clock without shortening the whole wait; the Budget Analyst makes the same point (median 280 days for housing permits, the longest of the cities it compared).","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"type","t":"Kind of permit","type":"text"},{"k":"year","t":"Year issued","type":"year"},{"k":"issued","t":"Permits issued","type":"int"},{"k":"median","t":"Median days","type":"int"},{"k":"p90","t":"Slowest tenth took at least (days)","type":"int"},{"k":"overYear","t":"Share over one year","type":"pct"},{"k":"sameDay","t":"Share issued within a day","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"type":"Alterations sent for full plan review","year":"2016","issued":1847,"median":228,"p90":617,"overYear":0.274,"sameDay":0.001},{"type":"Alterations sent for full plan review","year":"2017","issued":1651,"median":254,"p90":676,"overYear":0.314,"sameDay":0.0},{"type":"Alterations sent for full plan review","year":"2018","i